Also fix unused vars: `handleMarquee` unused in BoardWorkspace (I pass setMarquee directly), and `size` in BoardViewport.

For marquee: I want the selection logic on marquee end, but setMarquee for visual. Let me restructure: BoardViewport calls `onMarquee(rect|null)` continuously during move and at end. To keep it simple: viewport calls onMarquee on move (for visual + no selection) and at end calls `onMarqueeEnd(rect|null)`? The design of BoardViewport props has onMarquee only. Let me add an `onMarqueeEnd` prop: during move → onMarquee(rect), on end → onMarquee(null) + onMarqueeEnd(rect|null).

Simplest change: keep single callback but with a second arg `final: boolean`. I'll do that.

Update BoardViewport: `onMarquee?: (rect: Rect | null, final: boolean) => void`.
In BoardWorkspace:
```ts
const handleMarquee = (rect, final) => {
  if (!final) { setMarquee(rect); return; }
  setMarquee(null);
  if (!rect) { selection.clear(); return; }  // hmm clicking empty canvas clears selection? yes
  ...select intersecting
};
```
Note: click on empty canvas (moved<=3) → final rect null → clears selection. That's desirable.

Also remove unused `size` variable in BoardViewport.

