Wait: deleting navigator.clipboard after each test is tricky since jsdom defines navigator.clipboard? In jsdom, `navigator.clipboard` is undefined by default. Tests will define it with Object.defineProperty and configurable: true.

Now write pages.test.tsx (TC-16..TC-21).

TC-16: Home page renders correctly: heading "vidi6", tagline, button "Create a board".
TC-17: Create → error state → button re-enabled: mock api.createBoardRequest to return {kind:'failed'}; click → wait for error text; button enabled with "Create a board". Also rate_limited variant shows the rate-limit message.
TC-18: Board page loading → ready: mock checkBoard to resolve after a deferred; assert "Opening board…" first, then ready marker.
TC-19: /b/bad → NotFoundPage and checkBoard never called.
TC-20: NotFound page renders + create works: mock createBoardRequest resolves created with id; click "Create a new board" → navigate to /b/<id> → assert location and that the board route rendered.
TC-21: Board page retry backoff (2 fails then 200): use fake timers; mock checkBoard: unreachable, unreachable, exists. Assert "Couldn't reach vidi6. Retrying…" shown; advance timers by 1000 → second attempt; then 2000 → third attempt → ready. Assert delays of 1000 and 2000 (backoff).

For mocking, use `vi.mock('../../src/client/api', ...)`. Path must match how BoardPage imports it: '../api' from src/client/pages → resolves to /src/client/api. vi.mock path in the test file is resolved relative to the test file, so `vi.mock('../../src/client/api')` works (vitest resolves to the same module id).

Also `vi.mock('../../src/client/board/BoardWorkspace')`.

Navigation: jsdom URL is http://localhost:3000/ by default; use vi.stubEnv? Instead set the URL via `vi.stubGlobal`? For jsdom in vitest, configure `environmentOptions: { jsdom: { url: 'http://localhost/' } }`. Default is 'http://localhost:3000/'. Fine; window.location.origin = 'http://localhost:3000'.

For TC-20 and TC-17, navigate() changes the path; subsequent tests need the location reset. jsdom keeps the same URL across tests in a file — since navigate uses pushState, the path persists between tests in the same file. To keep tests independent, each test should reset with `window.history.replaceState({}, '', '/')` in beforeEach... but the router's listeners rely on popstate; replaceState won't trigger re-render, but we mount fresh each test, so the initial read of location.pathname is fine.

Careful for TC-19: the route id comes from App; but I render `<BoardPage id="bad" />` directly for TC-19 (design says component test of the board page with malformed id). Simpler: render App with a path set. I'll render `<BoardPage id="not-valid" />` and assert NotFoundPage content + checkBoard not called.

TC-18: render `<BoardPage id={validId} />` with mocked checkBoard deferred.

Also assert BoardWorkspace receives the id.

Fake timers + React 19 + testing-library: use `await act(async () => { vi.advanceTimersByTime(...) })`. With fake timers, `waitFor` from RTL works if we advance timers. Let me write TC-21 carefully:

```ts
vi.useFakeTimers();
const checkBoard = ...; // mock returns unreachable, unreachable, exists
render(<BoardPage id={id} />);
await waitFor(() => expect(checkBoard).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1));
expect(screen.getByText("Couldn't reach vidi6. Retrying…")).toBeInTheDocument();
await act(async () => { vi.advanceTimersByTime(1000); });
expect(checkBoard).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);
await act(async () => { vi.advanceTimersByTime(1000); });  // 2000 total, second retry not yet fired
expect(checkBoard).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);
await act(async () => { vi.advanceTimersByTime(1000); });
expect(checkBoard).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(3);
await waitFor(() => expect(screen.getByTestId('board-workspace')).toBeInTheDocument());
vi.useRealTimers();
```
Careful: mocked promise resolution inside act with fake timers — `await act(async () => {...})` flushes microtasks ✓.

Note the promise chain: `run()` awaits checkBoard (a promise resolved immediately by the mock) — resolution happens on the microtask queue, so after `await waitFor(...)` it's processed.

